1
00:03:08,640 --> 00:03:10,520
Where is that shameless daughter-in-law?

2
00:03:10,600 --> 00:03:13,640
<i>I think Hathai
might be sleeping with Dech.</i>

3
00:03:13,720 --> 00:03:17,200
Both of my sons died because of you.

4
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:18,960
PREVIOUSLY

5
00:03:19,040 --> 00:03:22,080
<i>Hathaya, please find
the money to pay off my debt.</i>

6
00:03:22,160 --> 00:03:24,080
<i>Where am I supposed
to get that kind of money?</i>

7
00:03:24,680 --> 00:03:25,960
<i>Go see your father. Go see Grandpa.</i>

8
00:03:26,040 --> 00:03:29,560
<i>Bring back the money
so we can pay for Grandma's treatment.</i>

9
00:03:33,720 --> 00:03:35,000
Have we met before?

10
00:03:36,400 --> 00:03:37,520
Grandpa.

11
00:03:39,600 --> 00:03:40,800
My name is Hathaya.

12
00:03:50,560 --> 00:03:51,920
I missed you so much, Grandpa.

13
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:54,120
I love you more than anyone in the world.

14
00:04:01,360 --> 00:04:02,640
You're not my granddaughter.

15
00:04:10,240 --> 00:04:12,480
I'm Hathaya, Grandpa.

16
00:04:13,160 --> 00:04:14,880
I'm your granddaughter.

17
00:04:15,640 --> 00:04:19,200
My granddaughter died
along with that wicked mother of hers.

18
00:04:20,120 --> 00:04:21,320
They're both dead to me.

19
00:04:27,080 --> 00:04:29,720
I know what my mom did,

20
00:04:30,520 --> 00:04:32,880
and I know how angry you are with her.

21
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:35,520
But I wanted to come back to you.

22
00:04:37,600 --> 00:04:39,080
You wanted to come back to me,

23
00:04:39,960 --> 00:04:42,840
yet you let more than ten years go by?

24
00:04:44,360 --> 00:04:46,280
Mom wouldn't let me come here.

25
00:04:46,920 --> 00:04:49,640
She told me this house had burned down

26
00:04:49,720 --> 00:04:51,120
and everyone who lived here

27
00:04:52,040 --> 00:04:53,680
had died.

28
00:04:54,640 --> 00:04:56,280
Your mother is evil.

29
00:04:56,360 --> 00:04:58,320
She practically cursed me to my grave.

30
00:05:02,280 --> 00:05:04,160
That cruelty is simply in her nature.

31
00:05:08,400 --> 00:05:11,520
Please let me apologize
on behalf of her, Grandpa.

32
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:15,200
I only just found out the truth myself.

33
00:05:15,280 --> 00:05:16,960
Once I learned
that everyone was still here,

34
00:05:17,640 --> 00:05:19,200
I rushed back

35
00:05:19,720 --> 00:05:21,600
because I missed you.

36
00:05:21,680 --> 00:05:22,920
I missed Dad too.

37
00:05:23,840 --> 00:05:25,560
Where is my dad?

38
00:05:36,320 --> 00:05:39,640
Aunt Liu, where is my dad?

39
00:05:41,440 --> 00:05:42,760
Your dad is dead.

40
00:05:46,360 --> 00:05:49,240
Back then, Burapha and my husband

41
00:05:49,320 --> 00:05:52,320
went after you to bring you back.
They got into an accident.

42
00:05:53,760 --> 00:05:55,840
They died because of you.

43
00:06:01,360 --> 00:06:03,560
I'm sorry, Aunt Liu.

44
00:06:05,040 --> 00:06:08,040
Chaya, I'm sorry.

45
00:06:12,800 --> 00:06:15,280
I lost both of my sons.

46
00:06:16,720 --> 00:06:19,640
Do you have any idea how much I lost?

47
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:24,000
Do you know how long it took us

48
00:06:25,480 --> 00:06:27,520
to put those horrible memories behind us?

49
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:32,040
And then suddenly

50
00:06:32,720 --> 00:06:34,440
you show up on what was supposed to be

51
00:06:34,520 --> 00:06:36,920
one of the happiest days of my life.

52
00:06:38,320 --> 00:06:41,360
You're just as terrible
as your mother. You're selfish!

53
00:06:45,960 --> 00:06:48,080
Ever since the day
you two left this house,

54
00:06:49,160 --> 00:06:51,080
we considered you dead.

55
00:06:57,760 --> 00:06:59,200
So consider us dead too.

56
00:06:59,840 --> 00:07:02,080
In this life or the next,
I never want to see you.

57
00:07:06,240 --> 00:07:08,720
Whatever debt we had
to each other ends here.

58
00:07:11,120 --> 00:07:13,400
Get out. Get out!

59
00:07:17,720 --> 00:07:20,680
I know how much everyone has suffered.

60
00:07:22,120 --> 00:07:24,000
But I want you to know

61
00:07:24,520 --> 00:07:27,600
that I've suffered just as much
as you have, Grandpa.

62
00:07:29,240 --> 00:07:31,640
Back then, all I could do was cry for you.

63
00:07:32,840 --> 00:07:34,400
I wanted to come home.

64
00:07:37,120 --> 00:07:38,680
But I was only a child.

65
00:07:39,520 --> 00:07:41,200
There was nothing I could do.

66
00:07:44,520 --> 00:07:46,440
You hate my mother.

67
00:07:47,720 --> 00:07:49,400
But am I also to blame

68
00:07:50,240 --> 00:07:52,440
just because I'm her daughter?

69
00:07:56,600 --> 00:07:58,040
Grandpa,

70
00:07:58,560 --> 00:08:01,440
no one chooses to be born
into a broken family.

71
00:08:02,280 --> 00:08:05,240
And no one wants to have a bad mother.

72
00:08:10,880 --> 00:08:14,120
If you don't want me, that's okay.

73
00:08:14,840 --> 00:08:15,920
I'll leave.

74
00:08:17,560 --> 00:08:19,760
But I want you to know that

75
00:08:20,280 --> 00:08:22,880
no matter how much time passes,

76
00:08:24,080 --> 00:08:26,040
I will always love you.

77
00:08:27,360 --> 00:08:29,760
And I will always be your granddaughter.

78
00:08:50,080 --> 00:08:51,200
Father!

79
00:08:51,280 --> 00:08:52,800
- Grandpa!
- Father!

80
00:08:52,880 --> 00:08:54,760
Father!

81
00:08:54,840 --> 00:08:56,400
- Call an ambulance.
- Grandpa!

82
00:08:58,720 --> 00:08:59,600
Oh, Father.

83
00:09:09,840 --> 00:09:12,400
Wait. I think you should go home.

84
00:09:13,560 --> 00:09:15,000
Please let me see Grandpa.

85
00:09:16,280 --> 00:09:17,240
Hey.

86
00:09:17,760 --> 00:09:19,440
I'm warning you because I mean well.

87
00:09:19,960 --> 00:09:22,720
Ms. Liu is furious with you.
She doesn't want to see you.

88
00:09:23,800 --> 00:09:26,240
Please let me visit Grandpa.

89
00:09:26,760 --> 00:09:29,280
I just want to see him.
If Grandpa is okay,

90
00:09:29,360 --> 00:09:30,800
I won't bother them again.

91
00:09:31,800 --> 00:09:33,960
Please. I'm really worried about him.

92
00:09:34,040 --> 00:09:36,360
Please. Can I?

93
00:09:37,960 --> 00:09:38,880
Please.

94
00:09:46,960 --> 00:09:48,440
Go home!

95
00:09:53,760 --> 00:09:54,960
Aunt Liu,

96
00:09:55,480 --> 00:09:57,520
I'm really worried about Grandpa.

97
00:09:58,720 --> 00:09:59,920
Listen to me.

98
00:10:00,680 --> 00:10:03,320
Before this, Father was healthy

99
00:10:03,400 --> 00:10:04,640
and happy.

100
00:10:04,720 --> 00:10:06,520
But the moment you came into this house,

101
00:10:06,600 --> 00:10:09,040
everything went wrong.

102
00:10:09,120 --> 00:10:11,200
You only bring bad luck,
just like your mother.

103
00:10:13,440 --> 00:10:16,200
Father used to say your mother

104
00:10:16,280 --> 00:10:17,640
was a parasite

105
00:10:17,720 --> 00:10:20,280
who latched onto him and sucked him dry.

106
00:10:20,360 --> 00:10:21,720
And he was right.

107
00:10:21,800 --> 00:10:25,320
Your mother stole his money
and my jewelry.

108
00:10:25,840 --> 00:10:29,440
And now that she's lost everything,

109
00:10:29,520 --> 00:10:32,400
she sends you back here
to be another low-class parasite,

110
00:10:32,480 --> 00:10:35,360
clinging to us and sucking away
our blood and money.

111
00:10:35,440 --> 00:10:37,400
Tell me. Am I wrong?

112
00:10:49,800 --> 00:10:53,760
I know you love Grandpa, Hathaya,

113
00:10:54,360 --> 00:10:56,760
and I understand how you feel.

114
00:11:03,080 --> 00:11:04,680
But your mother

115
00:11:06,280 --> 00:11:08,360
hurt Grandpa deeply.

116
00:11:08,440 --> 00:11:10,760
She disappointed him
and caused him so much pain.

117
00:11:11,360 --> 00:11:13,120
And now Grandpa is sick too.

118
00:11:13,800 --> 00:11:15,400
I'm worried about his feelings.

119
00:11:22,880 --> 00:11:24,800
You say you love Grandpa.

120
00:11:25,720 --> 00:11:28,400
Then give him what he wants.

121
00:11:29,440 --> 00:11:31,320
Get out of his life.

122
00:11:31,840 --> 00:11:35,000
Consider it your birthday gift to him.

123
00:11:42,280 --> 00:11:43,280
Alright.

124
00:11:44,000 --> 00:11:45,280
I'll go.

125
00:11:47,280 --> 00:11:48,960
But Aunt Liu,

126
00:11:49,040 --> 00:11:51,320
could you please
tell Grandpa something for me?

127
00:11:55,400 --> 00:11:56,600
Tell him that I love him

128
00:11:57,840 --> 00:12:00,160
and that I've always missed him.

129
00:12:16,720 --> 00:12:18,680
Doctor, how is my grandfather?

130
00:12:27,640 --> 00:12:30,160
Hey, wait.

131
00:12:37,760 --> 00:12:38,920
The housekeeper knew

132
00:12:40,360 --> 00:12:41,840
you were coming to the hospital,

133
00:12:42,360 --> 00:12:44,680
so she brought your suitcase here for you.

134
00:12:45,640 --> 00:12:46,640
Here.

135
00:12:49,400 --> 00:12:50,560
Thank you.

136
00:12:52,040 --> 00:12:53,680
Where are you going?

137
00:13:00,800 --> 00:13:02,640
I came here

138
00:13:03,520 --> 00:13:06,800
because I love my grandpa and missed him.

139
00:13:09,880 --> 00:13:11,240
But unfortunately,

140
00:13:12,800 --> 00:13:14,680
my dad is gone.

141
00:13:16,760 --> 00:13:19,800
And Grandpa hates me
and is furious with me.

142
00:13:22,320 --> 00:13:24,080
So I'll go back to where I belong.

143
00:13:28,280 --> 00:13:30,000
Thank you

144
00:13:30,720 --> 00:13:32,920
for being kind to a parasite like me.

145
00:13:34,320 --> 00:13:35,840
I'm only one of his workers.

146
00:13:36,680 --> 00:13:37,920
I'm an outsider,

147
00:13:39,320 --> 00:13:41,120
so I can't meddle in your family.

148
00:13:43,800 --> 00:13:45,680
But as his granddaughter,

149
00:13:47,400 --> 00:13:48,560
you have the right to know

150
00:13:49,600 --> 00:13:51,320
what illness he has.

151
00:13:53,560 --> 00:13:54,800
What's wrong with Grandpa?

152
00:13:55,920 --> 00:13:57,440
Is it serious?

153
00:14:10,560 --> 00:14:12,720
Careful, Grandpa.

154
00:14:15,480 --> 00:14:18,640
I'm still strong. I can walk just fine.
Don't worry.

155
00:14:19,680 --> 00:14:20,840
Father,

156
00:14:20,920 --> 00:14:24,280
a stroke can be very dangerous.

157
00:14:24,360 --> 00:14:26,000
The doctor specifically told us

158
00:14:26,080 --> 00:14:28,720
that you need to be watched
very carefully.

159
00:14:28,800 --> 00:14:29,800
That's right.

160
00:14:29,880 --> 00:14:32,440
If your arms or legs suddenly become weak

161
00:14:32,520 --> 00:14:36,040
and you fall and hit your head,
it could be very dangerous.

162
00:14:36,120 --> 00:14:40,440
The MRI results just came back.
They said the narrowing is only minor.

163
00:14:40,520 --> 00:14:42,200
It's nothing serious.

164
00:14:42,280 --> 00:14:44,760
Besides, you just wished
for me to stay strong.

165
00:14:44,840 --> 00:14:46,560
Your wish is already

166
00:14:46,640 --> 00:14:48,400
working for me. See?

167
00:14:49,760 --> 00:14:50,960
Mom and I

168
00:14:51,040 --> 00:14:52,960
will take the best care of you, Grandpa.

169
00:14:53,040 --> 00:14:54,720
Alright, dear.

170
00:14:58,960 --> 00:15:01,760
Father, are you looking for someone?

171
00:15:02,360 --> 00:15:04,160
That woman went back already, didn't she?

172
00:15:06,360 --> 00:15:10,840
You can always tell whether someone
truly loves you when you're sick.

173
00:15:10,920 --> 00:15:13,360
If Hathaya really loved you,

174
00:15:13,440 --> 00:15:15,880
she would've stayed
by your side at the hospital.

175
00:15:15,960 --> 00:15:18,040
But what did she do?

176
00:15:18,120 --> 00:15:22,080
The moment she saw you collapse,
she grabbed her suitcase and ran away.

177
00:15:23,240 --> 00:15:24,680
Good. It's better that she left.

178
00:15:25,960 --> 00:15:27,880
Make sure everyone knows

179
00:15:27,960 --> 00:15:30,040
not to let her
set foot in this house again.

180
00:15:31,040 --> 00:15:32,680
Of course, Father.

181
00:15:34,360 --> 00:15:36,760
Get out! I told you
that you can't come in!

182
00:15:36,840 --> 00:15:39,040
I said you can't come in!

183
00:15:39,120 --> 00:15:40,240
Oh.

184
00:15:42,480 --> 00:15:44,440
- What is this?
- Hello, Grandpa.

185
00:15:48,200 --> 00:15:50,640
Hello, Aunt Liu. Hi, Chayanee.

186
00:15:52,480 --> 00:15:54,440
Why are you back?
You said you were leaving.

187
00:15:54,520 --> 00:15:56,800
I heard Grandpa is sick
and needs someone to care for him.

188
00:15:56,880 --> 00:16:00,160
So I packed my things
and came back to live here.

189
00:16:00,880 --> 00:16:03,280
Stay out of my business.
You're not a nurse.

190
00:16:04,160 --> 00:16:05,840
I didn't graduate from nursing school,

191
00:16:05,920 --> 00:16:08,480
but my maternal grandpa
had the same condition as you.

192
00:16:08,560 --> 00:16:11,360
I know how to take care
of someone after a stroke.

193
00:16:11,440 --> 00:16:14,720
Then where is your other grandpa?
Go take care of him.

194
00:16:14,800 --> 00:16:15,960
He passed away.

195
00:16:16,480 --> 00:16:18,160
But he died in an accident.

196
00:16:18,240 --> 00:16:20,240
Stay out of my business.

197
00:16:21,120 --> 00:16:22,600
Take your bags and leave.

198
00:16:23,560 --> 00:16:24,640
I've never had

199
00:16:24,720 --> 00:16:28,000
the chance to repay you
for everything you did for me.

200
00:16:28,080 --> 00:16:31,560
Please let me use this opportunity
to make up for all the years we lost.

201
00:16:32,880 --> 00:16:34,160
You really are stubborn.

202
00:16:34,240 --> 00:16:35,600
If you refuse to listen,

203
00:16:35,680 --> 00:16:39,200
I'll call the police
and have them drag you out of here.

204
00:16:39,280 --> 00:16:42,080
Aunt Liu, I'm Grandpa's
own flesh and blood.

205
00:16:42,160 --> 00:16:43,640
Please let me stay here

206
00:16:43,720 --> 00:16:45,880
so I can repay you both
for everything you've done.

207
00:16:47,920 --> 00:16:50,440
What do you really want
by coming back here?

208
00:16:51,920 --> 00:16:54,840
Your mother is out of options,
so she sent you back, right?

209
00:16:57,400 --> 00:16:58,240
Yes.

210
00:17:00,320 --> 00:17:02,560
See, Father? I knew it.

211
00:17:02,640 --> 00:17:04,480
Her mother sent her back here

212
00:17:04,560 --> 00:17:07,119
to suck you dry again.

213
00:17:10,720 --> 00:17:13,839
I admit that I'm in trouble, Grandpa.

214
00:17:14,640 --> 00:17:16,319
I need one million baht.

215
00:17:16,400 --> 00:17:18,520
Mom owes money to illegal lenders.

216
00:17:20,240 --> 00:17:22,720
If we don't pay them,
they're going to kill her.

217
00:17:23,440 --> 00:17:24,960
And my grandma is seriously ill.

218
00:17:25,480 --> 00:17:27,800
I need money for her treatment too.

219
00:17:30,480 --> 00:17:32,440
How pathetic.

220
00:17:32,520 --> 00:17:35,960
So your true colors finally come out. You
came because you're desperate for money.

221
00:17:36,560 --> 00:17:38,800
But fine, since we're family,

222
00:17:38,880 --> 00:17:42,840
I'll give you money for the trip home.
Then never set foot here again.

223
00:17:43,480 --> 00:17:45,280
- Chamoi.
- Yes, ma'am?

224
00:17:45,360 --> 00:17:46,280
Drag her bags outside.

225
00:17:46,360 --> 00:17:48,120
Yes, ma'am.

226
00:17:48,200 --> 00:17:49,800
Please don't, Aunt Chamoi. No!

227
00:17:49,880 --> 00:17:51,040
Don't take my things.

228
00:17:51,120 --> 00:17:52,920
No, please!

229
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:54,360
Stop.

230
00:17:55,680 --> 00:17:58,760
Father, don't give in to her.

231
00:18:03,960 --> 00:18:05,320
I have an offer for you.

232
00:18:08,640 --> 00:18:10,160
You said you need money.

233
00:18:10,880 --> 00:18:12,240
Then I'll hire you to work.

234
00:18:16,880 --> 00:18:19,600
I'll give you 500,000 baht now.

235
00:18:21,640 --> 00:18:25,200
Work for me for one month,
and I'll give you another 500,000.

236
00:18:30,440 --> 00:18:33,520
Or there's another offer.
An even better one.

237
00:18:35,800 --> 00:18:38,400
Take ten million baht
and never set foot here again.

238
00:18:48,680 --> 00:18:49,720
Grandpa,

239
00:18:50,840 --> 00:18:53,920
I am in trouble. And I do need the money.

240
00:18:58,520 --> 00:19:01,200
But I will not walk out of your life.

241
00:19:04,520 --> 00:19:06,600
I'll work for you.

242
00:19:06,680 --> 00:19:08,600
Whatever job you give me,

243
00:19:09,560 --> 00:19:12,360
I'll do it for the entire month.

244
00:19:12,440 --> 00:19:15,480
I'll prove to you that I truly love you.

245
00:19:16,600 --> 00:19:18,240
Don't just talk big.

246
00:19:19,040 --> 00:19:21,480
If you slack off or miss
even a single day of work,

247
00:19:22,320 --> 00:19:24,640
you won't receive
a single baht of the rest.

248
00:19:25,520 --> 00:19:26,440
Alright.

249
00:19:26,960 --> 00:19:29,960
I'll prove to you that I'm not a parasite.

250
00:19:36,520 --> 00:19:38,240
Which way are the workers' quarters?

251
00:19:38,320 --> 00:19:39,440
This way, miss.

252
00:19:39,520 --> 00:19:40,440
Let me help you.

253
00:19:40,520 --> 00:19:41,600
No one helps her.

254
00:19:42,120 --> 00:19:45,280
Hathaya will live in this house
as a servant and worker.

255
00:19:45,360 --> 00:19:47,040
She has no privileges whatsoever.

256
00:19:49,560 --> 00:19:51,920
And if anyone helps this woman,

257
00:19:52,000 --> 00:19:53,400
I'll fire them immediately.

258
00:20:18,720 --> 00:20:20,000
Grandpa,

259
00:20:20,760 --> 00:20:22,960
did you let Hathaya stay

260
00:20:23,040 --> 00:20:25,920
because she's your own flesh and blood?

261
00:20:26,520 --> 00:20:27,840
At the very least,

262
00:20:27,920 --> 00:20:30,480
I can do this for my son.

263
00:20:30,560 --> 00:20:31,640
For Burapha.

264
00:20:35,800 --> 00:20:37,280
Father,

265
00:20:37,360 --> 00:20:39,080
if you want to help her,

266
00:20:39,160 --> 00:20:41,280
just give her the money and throw her out.

267
00:20:41,800 --> 00:20:44,760
She has no right to demand
anything from us anyway.

268
00:20:45,360 --> 00:20:47,680
I can see the same arrogance
and insolence in her

269
00:20:48,520 --> 00:20:49,960
that her mother had.

270
00:20:55,360 --> 00:20:57,680
I'm going to teach her pain and suffering

271
00:20:57,760 --> 00:20:59,880
far worse than anything
her mother ever put me through.

272
00:21:08,520 --> 00:21:10,280
I don't agree with this at all.

273
00:21:11,280 --> 00:21:13,440
Bringing a poisonous snake
this close to us?

274
00:21:13,520 --> 00:21:15,320
One day, it's going bite.

275
00:21:17,160 --> 00:21:19,720
Fine. I'll go throw her out myself.

276
00:21:20,320 --> 00:21:21,680
Don't, Mom.

277
00:21:23,640 --> 00:21:25,200
After all,

278
00:21:25,840 --> 00:21:27,640
Hathaya is still my sister.

279
00:21:42,120 --> 00:21:43,120
This is the room.

280
00:21:43,200 --> 00:21:44,160
All right.

281
00:21:55,280 --> 00:21:56,600
Thank you, Aunt Ann.

282
00:21:59,000 --> 00:22:01,280
Workers' rooms are pretty basic.

283
00:22:01,800 --> 00:22:04,240
There aren't many comforts here.

284
00:22:04,320 --> 00:22:05,680
Will you be alright?

285
00:22:06,360 --> 00:22:08,200
I'll be fine, Aunt Ann.

286
00:22:08,280 --> 00:22:11,560
When I lived in the countryside,
things were much harder than this.

287
00:22:11,640 --> 00:22:13,960
I feel so sorry for you.

288
00:22:14,720 --> 00:22:17,680
It's okay, Aunt Ann. I really can manage.

289
00:22:18,200 --> 00:22:19,480
And

290
00:22:19,560 --> 00:22:22,400
I think you should stop
being so polite to me.

291
00:22:22,480 --> 00:22:24,400
Aunt Liu and Grandpa might not like it.

292
00:22:25,000 --> 00:22:26,880
But I love you.

293
00:22:27,400 --> 00:22:29,720
I raised you ever since you were little.

294
00:22:31,760 --> 00:22:34,720
Still, when they're around,

295
00:22:34,800 --> 00:22:36,480
I'll be careful about what I say to you.

296
00:22:37,080 --> 00:22:39,280
Wait here for a moment.

297
00:22:39,360 --> 00:22:41,560
I'll go get you some necessities.

298
00:22:41,640 --> 00:22:43,160
Thank you, Aunt Ann.

299
00:23:06,400 --> 00:23:07,960
Aunt Ann, are you back already?

300
00:23:09,200 --> 00:23:10,200
Chaya.

301
00:23:11,240 --> 00:23:13,400
Hathaya,

302
00:23:14,120 --> 00:23:16,240
come with me.

303
00:23:16,760 --> 00:23:18,320
I'll go tell Grandpa

304
00:23:18,400 --> 00:23:21,840
to move my beloved big sister
into the main house.

305
00:23:22,520 --> 00:23:23,960
And if Grandpa refuses,

306
00:23:24,800 --> 00:23:26,680
then I'll move in here with you instead.

307
00:23:28,320 --> 00:23:31,040
Chaya, it's okay.

308
00:23:32,200 --> 00:23:33,400
I can stay here.

309
00:23:34,600 --> 00:23:37,200
- But--
- I understand how Grandpa feels.

310
00:23:38,440 --> 00:23:41,160
My mom hurt him deeply.

311
00:23:42,400 --> 00:23:45,880
And your dad died

312
00:23:45,960 --> 00:23:47,480
because of us.

313
00:23:49,280 --> 00:23:50,880
Please forgive me, Chaya.

314
00:24:01,200 --> 00:24:02,440
It's okay.

315
00:24:03,520 --> 00:24:05,400
That happened a long time ago.

316
00:24:06,520 --> 00:24:09,200
I've never been angry with you, Hathaya.

317
00:24:13,320 --> 00:24:16,600
The kinder you are to me,
the guiltier I feel.

318
00:24:18,600 --> 00:24:20,280
I'm willing to do anything

319
00:24:21,240 --> 00:24:24,000
to make up for my mom's mistakes.

320
00:24:24,600 --> 00:24:26,160
I'll prove to everyone

321
00:24:26,240 --> 00:24:28,200
that I came here because of love.

322
00:24:28,720 --> 00:24:30,920
I'm not here because
I want anything from Grandpa.

323
00:24:31,960 --> 00:24:35,520
Thank you so much
for understanding me, Chaya.

324
00:24:40,160 --> 00:24:41,880
We're sisters after all.

325
00:24:53,480 --> 00:24:54,720
- Chamoi.
- Ma'am.

326
00:24:54,800 --> 00:24:56,000
Wait.

327
00:24:57,760 --> 00:24:59,800
Those belong to Chayanee.

328
00:24:59,880 --> 00:25:01,800
Those belong to my girl.
Are you stealing them?

329
00:25:01,880 --> 00:25:02,760
Yes.

330
00:25:04,240 --> 00:25:05,920
No, no. I mean no!

331
00:25:06,000 --> 00:25:08,000
Of course not!

332
00:25:08,080 --> 00:25:10,840
I can see you carrying
my daughter's things out with my own eyes.

333
00:25:11,680 --> 00:25:12,880
Madam.

334
00:25:13,400 --> 00:25:14,600
I swear!

335
00:25:14,680 --> 00:25:18,200
Buddha, Dharma, Sangha. May lightning
strike your house if I'm lying!

336
00:25:18,280 --> 00:25:19,640
I didn't steal anything.

337
00:25:19,720 --> 00:25:22,960
I told Aunt Chamoi
to take those things to Hathaya.

338
00:25:23,880 --> 00:25:24,960
Go ahead.

339
00:25:25,040 --> 00:25:26,160
Yes, miss.

340
00:25:32,880 --> 00:25:34,480
Why are you helping her?

341
00:25:35,240 --> 00:25:36,800
If she gets too comfortable here,

342
00:25:36,880 --> 00:25:39,120
she'll cling to Grandpa
for the rest of her life.

343
00:25:40,840 --> 00:25:41,880
Listen to me.

344
00:25:42,960 --> 00:25:44,560
If she weren't here,

345
00:25:45,080 --> 00:25:48,280
all of Grandpa's inheritance
would belong to you.

346
00:25:48,840 --> 00:25:52,520
Are you going to let some selfish woman
come and take your inheritance away?

347
00:25:55,160 --> 00:25:56,320
Mom.

348
00:25:56,920 --> 00:25:58,280
What belongs to me stays mine.

349
00:25:58,960 --> 00:26:00,560
I won't let anyone take it from me.

350
00:26:02,320 --> 00:26:05,840
Then why are you being nice to her?
I don't understand.

351
00:26:09,240 --> 00:26:11,040
I'm going to make her trust me.

352
00:26:12,400 --> 00:26:15,120
I'll play the part
of the sweet little angel.

353
00:26:16,000 --> 00:26:17,400
And when the time comes,

354
00:26:18,320 --> 00:26:20,200
I'll drag her straight down to hell.

355
00:26:27,680 --> 00:26:30,040
I waited for Dad to come home.

356
00:26:34,400 --> 00:26:36,960
But they took him away from me.

357
00:26:51,640 --> 00:26:53,440
They're going to pay

358
00:26:54,920 --> 00:26:56,560
for what they did to our family.

359
00:27:37,200 --> 00:27:39,440
How are things over there?
Are they giving you the money?

360
00:27:40,040 --> 00:27:41,960
Grandpa is giving me 500,000 baht.

361
00:27:42,040 --> 00:27:44,040
Why did you only ask for that much?

362
00:27:44,120 --> 00:27:46,680
Why didn't you ask for ten or 20 million?

363
00:27:47,280 --> 00:27:48,200
Mom.

364
00:27:48,720 --> 00:27:50,960
You already stole so much money
and jewelry from them.

365
00:27:51,800 --> 00:27:53,360
<i>I don't want to bother Grandpa anymore.</i>

366
00:27:53,440 --> 00:27:57,560
The only reason I asked him for money
is so you can pay off your debt

367
00:27:57,640 --> 00:27:59,120
and pay for Grandma's treatment.

368
00:28:00,160 --> 00:28:01,400
Fine.

369
00:28:01,480 --> 00:28:04,560
And don't tell them where I am,

370
00:28:04,640 --> 00:28:06,280
or they'll call the police on me.

371
00:28:07,640 --> 00:28:08,560
Okay.

372
00:28:10,000 --> 00:28:12,320
Mom. How's Grandma?

373
00:28:14,560 --> 00:28:16,320
She's fine now.

374
00:28:16,400 --> 00:28:19,120
The doctor says she can leave
the hospital in a few days.

375
00:28:19,960 --> 00:28:23,240
Listen, tomorrow you need to hurry up
and get that money from them.

376
00:28:23,320 --> 00:28:25,560
Otherwise, they're really
going to kill me.

377
00:28:29,080 --> 00:28:30,120
Alright.

378
00:28:31,120 --> 00:28:35,040
Once Grandpa transfers the money,
I'll send it to you.

379
00:28:35,840 --> 00:28:37,200
Make sure to pay off the debt.

380
00:28:37,280 --> 00:28:39,560
Yeah, I know.

381
00:28:41,080 --> 00:28:43,400
How are you doing over there?

382
00:28:43,480 --> 00:28:44,960
They're treating you well, right?

383
00:28:54,200 --> 00:28:55,240
Well...

384
00:28:58,360 --> 00:29:00,240
Everyone here

385
00:29:00,320 --> 00:29:04,120
was so excited and happy that I came back.

386
00:29:06,000 --> 00:29:08,000
Grandpa hugged me really tight.

387
00:29:09,800 --> 00:29:11,840
He told me how much he missed me.

388
00:29:15,520 --> 00:29:16,760
And...

389
00:29:17,720 --> 00:29:19,080
your father?

390
00:29:19,640 --> 00:29:21,440
Did he ask about me?

391
00:29:27,560 --> 00:29:29,120
Dad is dead, Mom.

392
00:29:36,640 --> 00:29:38,040
Dad and Uncle Thot

393
00:29:38,800 --> 00:29:41,680
died in an accident that same day.

394
00:29:49,040 --> 00:29:51,080
I guess this was all the time we had.

395
00:29:52,280 --> 00:29:54,920
Take care of yourself.

396
00:29:56,320 --> 00:29:57,560
Okay, Mom.

397
00:30:26,240 --> 00:30:27,360
Grandma.

398
00:30:32,560 --> 00:30:36,480
I'll endure this and keep working
until the end of the month.

399
00:30:36,560 --> 00:30:38,400
I'll do my very best.

400
00:30:39,360 --> 00:30:41,960
I'll bring the money back
for your treatment.

401
00:31:07,880 --> 00:31:09,160
I'll help Father.

402
00:31:09,800 --> 00:31:11,080
Father.

403
00:31:13,280 --> 00:31:16,120
I'm feeling better now.
There's no need to worry.

404
00:31:19,960 --> 00:31:22,120
That arrogant woman
left already, didn't she?

405
00:31:26,120 --> 00:31:28,840
She thought she could come back
and live comfortably here,

406
00:31:29,640 --> 00:31:31,320
but after just one night

407
00:31:32,600 --> 00:31:35,200
in the workers' quarters,
she packed up and ran away.

408
00:31:37,480 --> 00:31:39,120
Who are you talking about, Grandpa?

409
00:31:46,960 --> 00:31:49,520
I hired you to work. Why are you late?

410
00:31:50,280 --> 00:31:54,280
I'm not late, Grandpa.
I know what time you eat,

411
00:31:54,360 --> 00:31:56,640
so I came to prepare
some hot rice porridge for you.

412
00:31:57,160 --> 00:31:59,080
You don't have to do that.

413
00:31:59,160 --> 00:32:01,840
Chamoi already prepared Father's food.

414
00:32:02,440 --> 00:32:05,600
Aunt Liu, Grandpa needs to watch his diet.

415
00:32:05,680 --> 00:32:08,320
He needs less salt, less fat,
and less strongly seasoned food.

416
00:32:08,400 --> 00:32:10,520
Aunt Chamoi used minced pork belly

417
00:32:10,600 --> 00:32:13,000
with fish sauce, sugar,
and seasoning sauce.

418
00:32:13,080 --> 00:32:17,360
I used lean pork and low-sodium
seasoning sauce instead.

419
00:32:17,440 --> 00:32:20,400
And this is vegetable juice, Grandpa.
It'll give you more fiber.

420
00:32:20,480 --> 00:32:23,400
I also don't recommend
drinking sweet fruit juice

421
00:32:23,480 --> 00:32:26,720
because it contains a lot of sugar,
which can affect your circulation.

422
00:32:27,240 --> 00:32:28,680
Enjoy your meal, Grandpa.

423
00:32:32,520 --> 00:32:34,600
Go make me another bowl. I'll wait.

424
00:32:34,680 --> 00:32:36,000
Yes, sir.

425
00:32:44,640 --> 00:32:46,320
Grandpa,

426
00:32:46,400 --> 00:32:48,920
Hathaya made this especially for you.

427
00:32:49,000 --> 00:32:52,800
You need to eat on time
so you can take your medicine.

428
00:32:56,680 --> 00:32:59,080
I already prepared
your after-meal medicine too.

429
00:33:00,440 --> 00:33:01,480
Please.

430
00:33:07,920 --> 00:33:09,440
If you're done, then go.

431
00:33:10,680 --> 00:33:12,520
There's plenty of work for you to do.

432
00:33:12,600 --> 00:33:14,920
Standing around here
is irritating me so much,

433
00:33:15,760 --> 00:33:16,800
I can't even eat.

434
00:33:25,960 --> 00:33:29,640
Hathaya, go get some rest.
I'll take care of Grandpa here.

435
00:33:39,800 --> 00:33:41,560
Come on, Grandpa. Eat.

436
00:33:44,200 --> 00:33:45,760
Let me help you.

437
00:33:45,840 --> 00:33:46,880
Chayanee.

438
00:34:47,280 --> 00:34:49,679
Here, miss. Let me do it.

439
00:34:49,760 --> 00:34:51,239
It's okay.

440
00:34:52,320 --> 00:34:53,440
I'll help.

441
00:34:54,159 --> 00:34:55,159
You don't have to.

442
00:34:55,760 --> 00:34:57,600
You've been up since early this morning,

443
00:34:57,680 --> 00:35:00,640
and you already cooked for Master.

444
00:35:00,720 --> 00:35:01,920
Go get some rest.

445
00:35:03,560 --> 00:35:04,600
You cannot rest.

446
00:35:05,600 --> 00:35:07,880
Madam ordered her to work.

447
00:35:07,960 --> 00:35:10,240
Chamoi, have you forgotten?

448
00:35:10,320 --> 00:35:13,600
This is Miss Hathaya.
She's one of our employers.

449
00:35:13,680 --> 00:35:17,440
I don't have Alzheimer's.
That was in the past.

450
00:35:17,520 --> 00:35:20,880
The Lord Buddha taught us

451
00:35:20,960 --> 00:35:22,520
not to cling to the past,

452
00:35:22,600 --> 00:35:26,360
not to worry about the future,

453
00:35:26,440 --> 00:35:29,200
but to live in the present.

454
00:35:29,280 --> 00:35:31,360
And right now,

455
00:35:31,440 --> 00:35:34,240
your precious Miss Hathaya is a servant.

456
00:35:34,320 --> 00:35:35,760
Madam specifically

457
00:35:35,840 --> 00:35:38,320
ordered me

458
00:35:38,400 --> 00:35:39,920
to keep an eye on her.

459
00:35:40,000 --> 00:35:42,800
I, Chamoi Sri,

460
00:35:42,880 --> 00:35:44,840
the loyal servant,

461
00:35:44,920 --> 00:35:47,560
must follow Madam's orders to the letter!

462
00:35:48,560 --> 00:35:50,880
You're nothing but a shameless suck-up.

463
00:35:50,960 --> 00:35:53,440
Whatever the master says,
the servant parrots.

464
00:35:53,520 --> 00:35:55,600
You keep pointing your finger in my face,

465
00:35:55,680 --> 00:35:56,880
- and I'm gonna slap you!
- Go ahead!

466
00:35:56,960 --> 00:35:58,360
Enough already.

467
00:35:58,440 --> 00:36:01,080
Stop!

468
00:36:01,160 --> 00:36:03,080
Don't fight because of me.

469
00:36:03,160 --> 00:36:04,160
I'll wash them myself.

470
00:36:04,240 --> 00:36:09,080
Applause, please! You are amazing.

471
00:36:11,360 --> 00:36:12,760
What is this?

472
00:36:13,800 --> 00:36:16,360
I washed these yesterday.

473
00:36:17,560 --> 00:36:18,800
Well, Madam said they weren't clean.

474
00:36:20,080 --> 00:36:21,400
And they stink.

475
00:36:21,480 --> 00:36:24,200
So she ordered everything
to be washed again.

476
00:36:26,040 --> 00:36:27,200
Just do it.

477
00:36:27,280 --> 00:36:31,560
Madam said they have to be washed
by hand until they're spotless.

478
00:36:32,360 --> 00:36:36,080
And don't let me catch you helping her.

479
00:36:36,160 --> 00:36:38,920
I'll tell Master and have you thrown out.

480
00:36:41,120 --> 00:36:43,480
Go on. Don't you have anything else to do?

481
00:36:47,440 --> 00:36:48,280
Shoo!

482
00:36:58,960 --> 00:37:00,840
Madam.

483
00:37:00,920 --> 00:37:02,720
- What?
- Madam.

484
00:37:02,800 --> 00:37:05,800
Madam, I gave her the full package.

485
00:37:05,880 --> 00:37:08,120
I made her wash all the clothes by hand,

486
00:37:08,200 --> 00:37:10,000
sweep and mop the floors,
hang up the laundry,

487
00:37:10,080 --> 00:37:11,320
clean the whole house.

488
00:37:11,400 --> 00:37:15,040
Now she's ironing until her hands
are practically twisted.

489
00:37:15,800 --> 00:37:17,640
Good.

490
00:37:17,720 --> 00:37:19,440
Do whatever it takes

491
00:37:19,520 --> 00:37:22,480
to make her leave this house
as soon as possible.

492
00:37:22,560 --> 00:37:24,240
I'll reward you handsomely.

493
00:37:24,320 --> 00:37:26,120
Madam,

494
00:37:26,200 --> 00:37:29,520
I already gave her the full package.

495
00:37:29,600 --> 00:37:31,840
So, I was thinking,

496
00:37:31,920 --> 00:37:34,080
maybe a little something for my trouble?

497
00:37:36,480 --> 00:37:38,360
- Here.
- Wow!

498
00:37:39,080 --> 00:37:39,920
Twenty baht?

499
00:37:40,520 --> 00:37:43,040
What? Is that too little for you?

500
00:37:44,040 --> 00:37:46,240
- You don't want it?
- Madam,

501
00:37:46,320 --> 00:37:49,960
seeing this makes my heart so full.

502
00:37:51,920 --> 00:37:53,880
I'm sleepy. I'm going to bed.

503
00:37:57,360 --> 00:38:00,520
She's a millionaire and tips me 20 baht.

504
00:38:00,600 --> 00:38:02,680
What a headache.

505
00:38:57,040 --> 00:38:59,040
<i>It's bedtime, Daddy's good girl.</i>

506
00:40:06,520 --> 00:40:08,000
Dad.

507
00:40:13,640 --> 00:40:15,160
I'm sorry.

508
00:40:17,960 --> 00:40:21,360
I'm sorry I made you leave us so soon.

509
00:40:31,680 --> 00:40:33,120
It wasn't your fault, sweetheart.

510
00:40:34,840 --> 00:40:36,600
Everything that happened.

511
00:40:37,520 --> 00:40:40,560
We can't turn back time to change it

512
00:40:40,640 --> 00:40:41,960
or fix it.

513
00:40:43,240 --> 00:40:44,880
But we can decide what to do now.

514
00:40:46,120 --> 00:40:47,840
When I came back here,

515
00:40:49,200 --> 00:40:53,120
I never imagined Grandpa would be
this angry with me and hate me this much.

516
00:40:54,480 --> 00:40:57,120
Do you love Grandpa?

517
00:41:00,080 --> 00:41:02,360
I love him very much.

518
00:41:04,880 --> 00:41:06,800
Then show him

519
00:41:06,880 --> 00:41:09,960
how much you love him.

520
00:41:16,000 --> 00:41:18,080
Don't worry about what anyone else says.

521
00:41:18,880 --> 00:41:24,080
In your heart, you know
what you're doing and why.

522
00:41:35,240 --> 00:41:36,720
Dad.

523
00:41:38,320 --> 00:41:39,880
I won't give up.

524
00:42:10,160 --> 00:42:11,640
My bedroom.

525
00:42:19,360 --> 00:42:20,440
Don't go in.

526
00:42:27,840 --> 00:42:32,600
I just wanted to see my old room.

527
00:42:34,200 --> 00:42:35,680
That is not your room.

528
00:42:36,640 --> 00:42:38,560
And I threw away
everything that was in it.

529
00:42:40,720 --> 00:42:44,480
When I was little,
you bought me a blanket.

530
00:42:44,560 --> 00:42:47,000
I wanted to go in
and get that old ragged blanket.

531
00:42:47,680 --> 00:42:49,280
I burned it.

532
00:42:52,600 --> 00:42:55,600
Why did you come upstairs?
Are you here to ask me for the money?

533
00:42:57,040 --> 00:42:58,000
No.

534
00:42:58,960 --> 00:43:01,320
I'll transfer the first 500,000 to you.

535
00:43:03,600 --> 00:43:05,840
But if you don't stay
until the end of the month,

536
00:43:07,560 --> 00:43:10,520
you won't get a single baht of the rest.
Don't forget that condition.

537
00:43:13,560 --> 00:43:14,960
And don't come upstairs again.

538
00:43:15,720 --> 00:43:18,000
You're a servant. Stay where you belong.

539
00:43:23,000 --> 00:43:24,040
Yes.

540
00:43:25,040 --> 00:43:26,040
Go.

541
00:44:21,800 --> 00:44:22,840
Hello, Mom.

542
00:44:23,720 --> 00:44:25,680
I already transferred 500,000 baht to you.

543
00:44:25,760 --> 00:44:27,880
Please hurry and pay off the debt

544
00:44:27,960 --> 00:44:30,040
before the interest gets even worse.

545
00:44:30,120 --> 00:44:34,280
Yeah, I know.
I'm not going to gamble with it.

546
00:44:34,800 --> 00:44:35,880
Bye.

547
00:44:35,960 --> 00:44:37,040
Bye.

548
00:44:46,920 --> 00:44:51,080
Like mother, like daughter.
You came to bleed me dry.

549
00:44:52,760 --> 00:44:55,560
I'll never forgive anyone
who was cruel to me.

550
00:45:02,360 --> 00:45:04,600
RAMIL

551
00:45:06,760 --> 00:45:10,240
Ramil. I need you to do something for me.

552
00:45:17,760 --> 00:45:18,600
You!

553
00:45:18,680 --> 00:45:21,040
Not "you". My name is Ramil.

554
00:45:21,120 --> 00:45:23,840
What the hell are you doing?
And how did you get in here?

555
00:45:23,920 --> 00:45:25,200
Spare key.

556
00:45:25,280 --> 00:45:28,160
Where did you get it?
And why did you throw water on me?

557
00:45:28,240 --> 00:45:30,200
It's part of my mission.

558
00:45:30,280 --> 00:45:33,760
Now get up, take a shower,
and get to work.

559
00:45:33,840 --> 00:45:36,200
Why should I listen to you?

560
00:45:36,280 --> 00:45:37,200
I'm not going.

561
00:45:42,040 --> 00:45:44,120
<i>Because it's my order.</i>

562
00:45:44,800 --> 00:45:45,640
Grandpa?

563
00:45:46,480 --> 00:45:48,120
I haven't been feeling well lately.

564
00:45:48,840 --> 00:45:51,600
I need to rest, so I don't have time
to go inspect the site.

565
00:45:52,240 --> 00:45:54,240
Ramil is my foreman.

566
00:45:55,720 --> 00:45:57,600
You'll be his helper.

567
00:45:57,680 --> 00:46:00,840
You want me to work with this rude man?

568
00:46:00,920 --> 00:46:03,680
He just barged into my room
and threw water on me!

569
00:46:05,000 --> 00:46:07,160
You think Ramil is rude?

570
00:46:07,920 --> 00:46:11,480
You barged into my birthday party
without being invited.

571
00:46:12,560 --> 00:46:14,200
My party was ruined because of you.

572
00:46:15,840 --> 00:46:17,600
Which one of you has worse manners?

573
00:46:22,320 --> 00:46:23,880
I'll go take a shower right now.

574
00:46:26,440 --> 00:46:28,120
Your tone changed pretty quickly.

575
00:46:28,200 --> 00:46:29,840
You've got ten minutes.

576
00:46:29,920 --> 00:46:31,320
Ten minutes?!

577
00:46:31,840 --> 00:46:33,360
Are you crazy? No way I can make it.

578
00:46:33,960 --> 00:46:36,280
Now you've got nine minutes
and 55 seconds.

579
00:46:44,280 --> 00:46:46,000
You jerk!

580
00:46:50,440 --> 00:46:51,480
I like hearing that.

581
00:46:51,560 --> 00:46:52,880
Why aren't you in the shower yet?

582
00:46:52,960 --> 00:46:55,560
Or do you want me to bathe you myself?

583
00:47:02,400 --> 00:47:05,920
Do you really want me to do that, sir?
She's your granddaughter.

584
00:47:06,520 --> 00:47:08,480
She was out of my life
for more than ten years.

585
00:47:09,520 --> 00:47:11,520
I have no idea what kind of person
she grew up to be

586
00:47:12,280 --> 00:47:14,320
or how her mother raised her.

587
00:47:17,120 --> 00:47:18,600
But if she wants to stay here,

588
00:47:19,120 --> 00:47:20,680
she has to prove to me

589
00:47:21,600 --> 00:47:23,560
that she's capable and sincere.

590
00:47:24,960 --> 00:47:26,000
Understood.

591
00:47:26,960 --> 00:47:28,440
I'll do exactly as you say.

592
00:47:32,000 --> 00:47:32,840
Grandpa,

593
00:47:33,600 --> 00:47:35,000
I'm ready for work.

594
00:47:38,400 --> 00:47:39,480
Go. The truck is waiting.

595
00:47:46,000 --> 00:47:46,960
Hathaya.

596
00:47:48,160 --> 00:47:49,480
If you can't handle it,

597
00:47:50,280 --> 00:47:52,960
have Ramil drive you
to the bus station and go back home.

598
00:47:57,640 --> 00:47:59,840
See you this evening, Grandpa.

599
00:48:11,480 --> 00:48:12,440
CONSTRUCTION PROJECT

600
00:48:14,320 --> 00:48:18,080
You're about to learn that a construction
worker's life isn't as easy as you think.

601
00:48:28,920 --> 00:48:31,360
Wait. What are you doing?

602
00:48:32,560 --> 00:48:33,880
Getting in.

603
00:48:37,160 --> 00:48:41,000
I shouldn't sit next to a rude driver.

604
00:48:41,080 --> 00:48:42,960
The boss should sit in the back.

605
00:48:44,000 --> 00:48:44,960
Wait. That's not it.

606
00:48:45,040 --> 00:48:47,200
In the truck bed.

607
00:48:47,280 --> 00:48:48,200
What?!

608
00:48:49,800 --> 00:48:52,240
You expect me to sit
in the back of the pickup?

609
00:48:52,320 --> 00:48:55,440
By the time we reach the site,
I'll be like a dried squid!

610
00:48:55,520 --> 00:48:56,680
I can't do that.

611
00:48:56,760 --> 00:49:00,760
If you can't handle it,
you're more than welcome to sit inside.

612
00:49:00,840 --> 00:49:03,040
I'll drive you straight
to the bus station.

613
00:49:21,200 --> 00:49:23,000
You lunatic!

614
00:49:23,520 --> 00:49:26,800
You are mean!
Couldn't you see I'd just climbed on?

615
00:49:27,560 --> 00:49:28,560
You!

616
00:49:38,040 --> 00:49:40,520
I haven't held 500,000 baht in years.

617
00:49:40,600 --> 00:49:42,320
My hands are shaking.

618
00:49:43,400 --> 00:49:44,360
Let me take another look.

619
00:50:10,120 --> 00:50:11,360
<i>Don't you dare!</i>

620
00:50:12,040 --> 00:50:15,080
<i>Grandpa sent her to work
at the construction site.</i>

621
00:50:15,160 --> 00:50:16,880
<i>I love it.</i>

622
00:50:16,960 --> 00:50:18,680
Working around construction workers?

623
00:50:18,760 --> 00:50:21,440
A few days and she'll probably
end up with a husband.

624
00:50:21,520 --> 00:50:22,880
<i>Go wash out the cement bucket.</i>

625
00:50:22,960 --> 00:50:24,160
NEXT EPISODE

626
00:50:24,240 --> 00:50:27,520
If I see even a trace of cement
left in it, you don't get to eat.

627
00:50:27,600 --> 00:50:29,440
Have you eaten anything yet?

628
00:50:32,120 --> 00:50:35,600
<i>How much longer are you
going to keep our secret?</i>

629
00:50:37,240 --> 00:50:40,880
Everything you've had since childhood
is because of me!

630
00:50:40,960 --> 00:50:43,320
Bring him here
and make him kneel before me!

631
00:50:43,400 --> 00:50:45,240
I'm not even sure

632
00:50:45,320 --> 00:50:46,800
he ever loved you, Mom.

633
00:51:46,760 --> 00:51:47,600
Subtitle translation by: Thanit Puncharoen
